WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.220 --> 00:00:10.440
Will technology revolutionize schooling?
Past efforts should leave us weary: the story

00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:15.400
of ed tech is one of over-promising
and under-delivering. To break this cycle,

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:19.640
we need to pay more attention to what
educators actually do with education

00:00:19.640 --> 00:00:25.160
technology. Yet major surveys of ed tech
use seem more interested in marketing

00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:29.840
than in making it work. Americans are
asked whether technology makes learning

00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:35.309
"easier and more fun," or whether they
think "AI could make a positive impact in

00:00:35.309 --> 00:00:39.899
the world of education." Teachers get
asked whether "using digital learning

00:00:39.899 --> 00:00:46.140
tools helps [them] teach more effectively."
And honestly, whatever the truth, are you

00:00:46.140 --> 00:00:51.780
going to be the Luddite who says "No"?
A better suggestion: Ask teachers how much

00:00:51.780 --> 00:00:55.980
time they spent dealing with
uncooperative technology, or whether

00:00:55.980 --> 00:01:00.980
their districts consider teacher input
when deciding what to buy. Digital learning

00:01:00.980 --> 00:01:05.840
has great promise, but achieving
it requires tending to the gritty reality,

00:01:05.840 --> 00:01:10.770
rather than uncritical cheerleading.
Have you seen an example of where

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:15.540
school technology actually got in the
way of learning? Let us know in our poll.

00:01:15.540 --> 00:01:19.320
Also let us know what other topics
you'd like our scholars to cover in 60

00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:23.250
seconds and be sure to LIKE and
subscribe for more research and videos

00:01:23.250 --> 00:01:26.000
from AEI.

